t","text":"85:**Limit kept.** A shell call that becomes write events hides any document read in the same call, which a redirect already does today: `cat <doc> > notes.md` prints `kinds=write startedCommand=null` (spec Measured Behavior). After this change `cat <doc> | tee notes.md` and `cp <doc> x.md` read the same way, and T003 pins that parity. Keeping a read beside the writes would also move every stored redirect run, so it is recorded in D13 rather than folded in.\n87:**Rejected.** Reading a Python, Node or other interpreter write. Its target is only known by running its code, so the `python write` line stays `kinds=shell`, recorded in D13. Treating every unknown shell call as a write, which would mark every `ls` unsafe.\n123:**Rejected.** Checking the four tracked absolute links under `specs/**/scratch`. They arrive through `git clone`, so `copyPath` never sees them (D13).\n169:### Decision D13: recorded, not built\n219:- Same-class producers: `rg -n \"new URL\\('\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./\\.\\./hooks/shared\" .skilled/skills --glob '*.ts' --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` lists the fixed-hop sources. One is built (T022) and the rest are recorded (D13). `rg -n \"'-Rc'|cp -R\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --glob '!**/node_modules/**'` lists every copy call.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"D13\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794780641443,"end":1794780643203}}}}
