{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794780930781,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1479e8a001CYLbofLZVVJHDi","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","messageID":"msg_1e1474158001YLHhRxkuivOV3F","type":"tool","id":"call_b67cb1c96f83440391d8bb38","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"install\\|truncate\\|rsync\\|git rm\\|xargs\\|-exec\\|target-directory\\|wrapped\\|writer\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-3.txt | head -40"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt:2:P2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1052 (Q2) nestedCommand looks for a shell name or `eval` anywhere in the segment with findIndex, not at the command position. So an argument word `eval` turns the rest of the segment into nested text. That drops writes the reader at d0f605b42f8 caught and adds writes to read-only commands. None of these are among the four allowed absences, which the T050c verifier names as the quoted git commit, the quoted tee, tee /dev/null and tee /dev/stderr. The round-two rescore is byte-identical to round one, so no stored run moved. | evidence: probe under mktemp in TMPDIR ran normalize on one Claude Bash call at BASE and FIX. Lost: `mkdir -p eval reports` BASE [\"eval\",\"reports\"] FIX [], `rm -rf eval out.json` BASE [\"eval\",\"out.json\"] FIX [], `touch eval notes.md` BASE [\"eval\",\"notes.md\"] FIX []. Added on read-only: `echo eval rm a.md` BASE [] FIX [\"a.md\"], `printf %s eval touch done.md` BASE [] FIX [\"done.md\"], `grep bash -c 'rm x.md'` BASE [] FIX [\"x.md\"], `bash script.sh -c 'rm x.md'` BASE [] FIX [\"x.md\"] | fix: read `eval` only as the segment's first word after assignments, and a shell name only there or after a known runner prefix (timeout N, env, sudo, nice, xargs), with one lost and one false case in the test table\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt:10:Q4: GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file broke nothing found. A local clone still works under it. Pi runs with --offline, which sets PI_OFFLINE, so package installs skip the network, and a failed package does not abort startup. The arena has no remote, so no live turn needs a network transport. Claude, Codex, OpenCode and Devin were graded from reading only. | evidence: `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=file git clone -q <src> <dst>` printed `plain-path clone ok exit=0`, and the file:// form also cloned. Pi 1.5.2 dist/main.js:494-496 and dist/core/package-manager.js:890 and :1124 read. Absolute links in the real copied trees: 18 ignored dist and node_modules trees, 110 links, 0 absolute, so T046 does not refuse the real arena\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-3.txt:2:P2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1104 (Q2) The eight wrapper forms read as no write at FIX. With no separator inside the nested text that matches d0f605b42f8, which read no write either. With a separator inside, BASE caught a garbled write through its plain split and FIX drops it, so the verifier's \"as before the rebuild\" holds only for the single-command form. That is the same class report-2 graded P2 for fish -c, ssh and watch, beside the accepted su -c case, so it is acceptable as a known limit. The limit is recorded only as one clause in the T050e evidence line, which names two of the eight forms, and not in plan D13 or any limits section. Against 02261e94254 this commit drops every one of these forms, which that commit read as writes, but the brief's reference is d0f605b42f8. | evidence: probe under mktemp in TMPDIR ran normalize on one Claude Bash call at d0f605b42f8 (BASE), 02261e94254 (MID) and d21dbc1cafe (FIX). `sudo bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `bash -o pipefail -c 'rm a.md'`, `timeout -k 2 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'`, `bash -O extglob -c`, `bash --rcfile f -c`, `bash +x -c`, `time -p bash -c`, `xargs bash -c`: each BASE [] MID [\"a.md\"] FIX []. `bash -o pipefail -c 'cd x; rm a.md'` and `sudo bash -c 'cd x; rm a.md'`: each BASE [\"a.md'\"] MID [\"x/a.md\"] FIX [] | fix: name the wrapper class (sudo, xargs, a shell option that takes a value, a runner option that takes a value) beside su -c in plan D13\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt:2:P2 .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1052 (Q2) nestedCommand looks for a shell name or `eval` anywhere in the segment with findIndex, not at the command position. So an argument word `eval` turns the rest of the segment into nested text. That drops writes the reader at d0f605b42f8 caught and adds writes to read-only commands. None of these are among the four allowed absences, which the T050c verifier names as the quoted git commit, the quoted tee, tee /dev/null and tee /dev/stderr. The round-two rescore is byte-identical to round one, so no stored run moved. | evidence: probe under mktemp in TMPDIR ran normalize on one Claude Bash call at BASE and FIX. Lost: `mkdir -p eval reports` BASE [\"eval\",\"reports\"] FIX [], `rm -rf eval out.json` BASE [\"eval\",\"out.json\"] FIX [], `touch eval notes.md` BASE [\"eval\",\"notes.md\"] FIX []. Added on read-only: `echo eval