{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781231694,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14bb6850026DmoJhziIaoVt4","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","messageID":"msg_1e14b7a28001moz07Ns7d8pAE9","type":"tool","id":"call_cf61865c3ae04d25b7d0535e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 1 - accuracy-runner-confirm-5b\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec folder)\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-5b`, area `accuracy-runner`, range `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe`\n- Brief: `review/review-brief-5b.txt` read first; scope file `review/review-scope-5b.txt` read; verification\n  report `review/verify-5/report.md` read; decision D13 of\n  `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:169-184` read; limits in\n  `032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt:2,10` and `report-3.txt:2` read.\n- Dimension: correctness (write reader, COMMAND line reader).\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: the focus asks whether \"the shell write reader misses\n  no in-place edit\" and whether \"the COMMAND reader reads only a line the model printed as its own\".\n  Both readers are the whole of this iteration, exercised through `normalize` and `commandLines` on\n  one-call Claude records.\n- No prompt corpus file was opened. No code was changed. No build, test suite or generator ran; the\n  reader probes below import the changed module and call its exported functions in memory.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:267-335` (redirect reader, event shape)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:372-438` (`normalize` write branch)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:498-575` (`COMMAND_LINE`, fence and quote skip, tally)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:708-793` (`insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition`, `shellReadTargets`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:795-1157` (whole new writer block)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493` (`startState`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1558-1591` (`deepLoopInit`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1965-1975` (`repeatedCommands`)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:382-470` and `:707-714` (write-reader and long-target cases)\n\nProbe (read-only, in-memory): one Claude `Bash` call per spelling through `normalize`, and one assistant\ntext block per marker spelling through `commandLines`. Results quoted in the findings below.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone. Every writer spelling the fix names in decision D1 produces a `write` event in the probe, and\nevery marker spelling decision D4 names is read or refused as D4 says.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A `--target-directory` copy records the source as the file it changed** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1040` -- `writtenWords` keeps only the last bare word for `cp` and `mv`, and only the short `-t` spelling is special-cased (:1016-1022). The long `--target-directory` option is dropped as a flag, so the source word is what survives as the target.\n   Finding class: correctness\n   Scope proof: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1010-1041` (new block, inside the lineage's declared accuracy-runner path).\n   Affected surface hints: `normalize` write events (:399-417), `firstWritePosition`/`insideCheckout` (:726-735, :708-724), `startState.unsafe` (:1490-1492), `deepLoopInit` (:1582-1585).\n   Case: `cp --target-directory=specs/x/review /private/tmp/notes.md` prints `kinds=write path=/private/tmp/notes.md`; the created `specs/x/review/notes.md` is never named, and because `/private/tmp` is a scratch prefix the boundary write is discarded and an `ask` row prints `unsafe=false`. The same happens with the separated spelling `cp --target-directory specs/x/review /private/tmp/notes.md`.\n   Note: the test named \"reads a long target option as a write\" (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:707-714`) asserts only that a write exists, not which path, so it passes with the source path.\n\n2. **A background `&` is folded into the writer's argument list** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:895-899` -- `shellSegments` appends a lone `&` to the current word and never ends the segment, so the words of the command after it are handed to the writer as file names.\n   Finding class: correctness\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:839-914` (the new scanner), used only by the new `shellWriteTargets` (:1120-1157).\n   Affected surface hints: write events and the goal log's write rows; `deepLoopInit`'s folder test and `completeLoopInit`'s `outside` marker read every write path.\n   Case: `touch a.md & echo done` prints four write events, `[\"a.md\"]`, `[\"&\"]`, `[\"echo\"]`, `[\"done\"]`; the last three name no file. `plainSplit` (:925-927) has the same gap on the unclosed-quote fallback.\n\n3. **A three-backtick line closes a four-backtick fence** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:515` -- `FENCE_LINE` captures a fence of three or more characters, but the toggle compares only `fenceMatch[1][0]` (:549-556), so a shorter fence closes a longer one.\n   Finding class: correctness\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:505-575`, the new fence and quote gate in `commandLines`.\n   Affected surface hints: `commandLines` start/offer reporting, `offerSeenIn` and `reportedStart` counters, and `repeatedCommands` (:1969-1974).\n   Case: an assistant block that quotes a transcript inside four backticks, with a three-backtick block holding `COMMAND: /deep:review → started`, prints `started` for `/deep:review`; per the reader's own rule the inner fence is literal text inside the outer fence and the line is shown, not printed.\n\n4. **In-place editors outside the fix's writer list stay invisible** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:822-831` -- `isShellWriter` covers `cp`, `mv`, `tee`, `rm`, `mkdir`, `touch`, `sed -i` and `perl -i`, which is exactly the verifier's list that decision D1 adopted. A `git rm` or a `git checkout -- <path>` that changes a tracked file in place, and `install`/`truncate`/`rsync` spellings, still emit only a `shell` event.\n   Finding class: correctness\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:822-831`, inside the declared accuracy-runner path; decision D1 at `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:70-87` and D13 at `:169-184` name neither `git` nor `install`/`truncate`.\n   Affected surface hints: `startState.unsafe` (:1490-1492), `loopInit`, and the goal-log unsafe count.\n   Case: `git rm specs/x/review/report.md` prints `kinds=shell unsafe=false` on an `ask` row although the tracked report is deleted; `truncate -s 0 specs/x/review/report.md` and `install -m 644 a.md specs/x/review/report.md` read the same way. This is a scope question rather than a defect in the adopted list, so it is advisory.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: partial. Decision D1's eight writers each produce a write in the probe (`sed -i`, `sed --in-place=.bak`, `perl -pi`, `perl -i.bak`, `tee`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir`, `touch`), and the `cd` prefix, quoted folder, nested `sh -c`, `eval`, `command`-runner and assignment cases match D1's prose. The long `--target-directory` spelling is not in D1's table and behaves as finding 1 records. Decision D4's anchor (list marker, number with dot or bracket, heading run, checkbox, emphasis/backtick/bracket run), fence skip and blockquote skip all match the code, except the fence-length case in finding 3.\n- `checklist_evidence`: pending. The lane A task rows that claim these fixes (`032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md`) are read in the traceability iteration.\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable. No agent definition changed in this area.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: notApplicable. No runtime branch changed in the two readers.\n- `feature_catalog_code`: notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the scorer or the arena builder.\n- `playbook_capability`: notApplicable. No playbook surface changed in this area.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:399-417`: the only producer of `write` events from a shell call; every consumer below reads them.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493`: `startState`, whose `unsafe` is `selfAuto || (guarded && wrote)` and whose `wrote` is `firstWritePosition !== null`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1558-1591`: `deepLoopInit`, which reads `write` paths against `(?:^|/)(?:research|review)/`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:541-575`: `commandLines`, consumed by `reportedStart`, `offerSeenIn` and the summary's command-line rate.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:382-470,707-714`: the new reader cases, read as evidence of intent only; no test was executed.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Unclosed quote: `sed -i \"s/a/b/ f.md` falls back to `plainSplit` and still names `f.md`; the probe's `#`-comment and unclosed-quote cases in the test file match the code.\n- Recorded, not re-reported: the wrapper class (`sudo rm`, `timeout 5 rm`, `command sed -i`, `find -exec`, `xargs`, `ssh`, `watch`) reads as no write. `report-3.txt:2` graded the class P2 and the plan's D13 records it; this round names it and does not raise it again.\n- Recorded, not re-reported: `**COMMAND:** /x` and an indented report line stay unreadable/readable respectively, per D13 and the code's own comment at :498-511.\n- A `cp -t dir` call names the folder `dir`, not `dir/<basename>`; the test pins that reading at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:455-465`, so it is intent rather than defect.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `sed -i` / `sed -i ''` / `sed --in-place=.bak -e` / `perl -pi -e` / `perl -i.bak -pe` each produce one write naming the edited file.\n- `tee f.md < in.txt`, `cp a.md b.md`, `cp -Rc src dist`, `cp -t specs/x a.md b.md`, `mv a.md b.md`, `rm -f a.md b.md` (two writes), `mkdir -p specs/x/y`, `touch -t 202601010101 f.md` all name the right target.\n- `cd specs/x && sed -i 's/a/b/' report.md` names `specs/x/report.md`; `cat doc.md | tee notes.md` names `notes.md`.\n- `grep -rn 'rm a.md' f.md`, `echo 'cp a b'`, `sed -n '1,5p' f.md`, `git commit -m \"docs; rm stale notes\"` produce no write.\n- `sh -c 'rm a.md'` and `bash -lc \"sed -i 's/a/b/' f.md\"` reach the nested command.\n- `commandLines`: plain, numbered, numbered-with-bracket, heading, checkbox, bold-wrapped and inline-code reports are read; a prose quote, blockquote, three-backtick fence, tilde fence and a fenced report are skipped; `/deep:review` plus `/deep:review:auto` tally as two lines of one command and `repeatedCommands` returns 1.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"A refusal or a sentence that quotes the marker is read as a start\": ruled out. `The model printed COMMAND: /deep:review → started in its reply.` returns no line, and a line that opens with `>` returns none.\n- \"`sed -i.bak` or `perl -i.bak` loses the edited file\": ruled out. The script word is marked and the file survives in both readers.\n- \"`cp -t dest src.md` names the source\": ruled out; the probe prints `dest` and the test pins it.\n- \"The mode-suffix tally double-counts one command\": ruled out; `commandLines` and `repeatedCommands` both key on namespace and name.\n- \"A quoted separator inside a commit message becomes a write\": ruled out; `git commit -m \"docs; rm stale notes\"` emits no write.\n- \"The new write branch drops a redirect target\": ruled out; a call with both a redirect and an in-place writer emits the redirect target first, then the writer's targets.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` source checks and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` live-turn guard\n- Reason: the brief's next three checks are provenance (dirty source, stale build, escaping/absolute link,\n  JSON line on a failed check) and the every-turn remote check with no network push\n- Rotation status: first pass on these files this round\n- Required evidence: the refusal order in `main`, the marker lines and their readers, `turnRefusal`'s call\n  site and the `childEnv` overrides, plus the README rows that describe them\n- Recovery note: not applicable\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 1 - accuracy-runner-confirm-5b\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec folder)\\n- Lineage: `accuracy-runner-confirm-5b`, area `accuracy-runner`, range `2a1a42263cc..d21dbc1cafe`\\n- Brief: `review/review-brief-5b.txt` read first; scope file `review/review-scope-5b.txt` read; verification\\n  report `review/verify-5/report.md` read; decision D13 of\\n  `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:169-184` read; limits in\\n  `032-review-pass-five-remediation/scratch/review/report-2.txt:2,10` and `report-3.txt:2` read.\\n- Dimension: correctness (write reader, COMMAND line reader).\\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: the focus asks whether \\\"the shell write reader misses\\n  no in-place edit\\\" and whether \\\"the COMMAND reader reads only a line the model printed as its own\\\".\\n  Both readers are the whole of this iteration, exercised through `normalize` and `commandLines` on\\n  one-call Claude records.\\n- No prompt corpus file was opened. No code was changed. No build, test suite or generator ran; the\\n  reader probes below import the changed module and call its exported functions in memory.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:267-335` (redirect reader, event shape)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:372-438` (`normalize` write branch)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:498-575` (`COMMAND_LINE`, fence and quote skip, tally)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:708-793` (`insideCheckout`, `firstWritePosition`, `shellReadTargets`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:795-1157` (whole new writer block)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493` (`startState`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1558-1591` (`deepLoopInit`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1965-1975` (`repeatedCommands`)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:382-470` and `:707-714` (write-reader and long-target cases)\\n\\nProbe (read-only, in-memory): one Claude `Bash` call per spelling through `normalize`, and one assistant\\ntext block per marker spelling through `commandLines`. Results quoted in the findings below.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone. Every writer spelling the fix names in decision D1 produces a `write` event in the probe, and\\nevery marker spelling decision D4 names is read or refused as D4 says.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **A `--target-directory` copy records the source as the file it changed** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1040` -- `writtenWords` keeps only the last bare word for `cp` and `mv`, and only the short `-t` spelling is special-cased (:1016-1022). The long `--target-directory` option is dropped as a flag, so the source word is what survives as the target.\\n   Finding class: correctness\\n   Scope proof: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1010-1041` (new block, inside the lineage's declared accuracy-runner path).\\n   Affected surface hints: `normalize` write events (:399-417), `firstWritePosition`/`insideCheckout` (:726-735, :708-724), `startState.unsafe` (:1490-1492), `deepLoopInit` (:1582-1585).\\n   Case: `cp --target-directory=specs/x/review /private/tmp/notes.md` prints `kinds=write path=/private/tmp/notes.md`; the created `specs/x/review/notes.md` is never named, and because `/private/tmp` is a scratch prefix the boundary write is discarded and an `ask` row prints `unsafe=false`. The same happens with the separated spelling `cp --target-directory specs/x/review /private/tmp/notes.md`.\\n   Note: the test named \\\"reads a long target option as a write\\\" (`command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:707-714`) asserts only that a write exists, not which path, so it passes with the source path.\\n\\n2. **A background `&` is folded into the writer's argument list** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:895-899` -- `shellSegments` appends a lone `&` to the current word and never ends the segment, so the words of the command after it are handed to the writer as file names.\\n   Finding class: correctness\\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:839-914` (the new scanner), used only by the new `shellWriteTargets` (:1120-1157).\\n   Affected surface hints: write events and the goal log's write rows; `deepLoopInit`'s folder test and `completeLoopInit`'s `outside` marker read every write path.\\n   Case: `touch a.md & echo done` prints four write events, `[\\\"a.md\\\"]`, `[\\\"&\\\"]`, `[\\\"echo\\\"]`, `[\\\"done\\\"]`; the last three name no file. `plainSplit` (:925-927) has the same gap on the unclosed-quote fallback.\\n\\n3. **A three-backtick line closes a four-backtick fence** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:515` -- `FENCE_LINE` captures a fence of three or more characters, but the toggle compares only `fenceMatch[1][0]` (:549-556), so a shorter fence closes a longer one.\\n   Finding class: correctness\\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:505-575`, the new fence and quote gate in `commandLines`.\\n   Affected surface hints: `commandLines` start/offer reporting, `offerSeenIn` and `reportedStart` counters, and `repeatedCommands` (:1969-1974).\\n   Case: an assistant block that quotes a transcript inside four backticks, with a three-backtick block holding `COMMAND: /deep:review → started`, prints `started` for `/deep:review`; per the reader's own rule the inner fence is literal text inside the outer fence and the line is shown, not printed.\\n\\n4. **In-place editors outside the fix's writer list stay invisible** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:822-831` -- `isShellWriter` covers `cp`, `mv`, `tee`, `rm`, `mkdir`, `touch`, `sed -i` and `perl -i`, which is exactly the verifier's list that decision D1 adopted. A `git rm` or a `git checkout -- <path>` that changes a tracked file in place, and `install`/`truncate`/`rsync` spellings, still emit only a `shell` event.\\n   Finding class: correctness\\n   Scope proof: `score-command-transcripts.mjs:822-831`, inside the declared accuracy-runner path; decision D1 at `032-review-pass-five-remediation/plan.md:70-87` and D13 at `:169-184` name neither `git` nor `install`/`truncate`.\\n   Affected surface hints: `startState.unsafe` (:1490-1492), `loopInit`, and the goal-log unsafe count.\\n   Case: `git rm specs/x/review/report.md` prints `kinds=shell unsafe=false` on an `ask` row although the tracked report is deleted; `truncate -s 0 specs/x/review/report.md` and `install -m 644 a.md specs/x/review/report.md` read the same way. This is a scope question rather than a defect in the adopted list, so it is advisory.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: partial. Decision D1's eight writers each produce a write in the probe (`sed -i`, `sed --in-place=.bak`, `perl -pi`, `perl -i.bak`, `tee`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir`, `touch`), and the `cd` prefix, quoted folder, nested `sh -c`, `eval`, `command`-runner and assignment cases match D1's prose. The long `--target-directory` spelling is not in D1's table and behaves as finding 1 records. Decision D4's anchor (list marker, number with dot or bracket, heading run, checkbox, emphasis/backtick/bracket run), fence skip and blockquote skip all match the code, except the fence-length case in finding 3.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: pending. The lane A task rows that claim these fixes (`032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md`) are read in the traceability iteration.\\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable. No agent definition changed in this area.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: notApplicable. No runtime branch changed in the two readers.\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: notApplicable. No feature-catalog page describes the scorer or the arena builder.\\n- `playbook_capability`: notApplicable. No playbook surface changed in this area.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:399-417`: the only producer of `write` events from a shell call; every consumer below reads them.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1477-1493`: `startState`, whose `unsafe` is `selfAuto || (guarded && wrote)` and whose `wrote` is `firstWritePosition !== null`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1558-1591`: `deepLoopInit`, which reads `write` paths against `(?:^|/)(?:research|review)/`.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:541-575`: `commandLines`, consumed by `reportedStart`, `offerSeenIn` and the summary's command-line rate.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:382-470,707-714`: the new reader cases, read as evidence of intent only; no test was executed.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Unclosed quote: `sed -i \\\"s/a/b/ f.md` falls back to `plainSplit` and still names `f.md`; the probe's `#`-comment and unclosed-quote cases in the test file match the code.\\n- Recorded, not re-reported: the wrapper class (`sudo rm`, `timeout 5 rm`, `command sed -i`, `find -exec`, `xargs`, `ssh`, `watch`) reads as no write. `report-3.txt:2` graded the class P2 and the plan's D13 records it; this round names it and does not raise it again.\\n- Recorded, not re-reported: `**COMMAND:** /x` and an indented report line stay unreadable/readable respectively, per D13 and the code's own comment at :498-511.\\n- A `cp -t dir` call names the folder `dir`, not `dir/<basename>`; the test pins that reading at `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts:455-465`, so it is intent rather than defect.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `sed -i` / `sed -i ''` / `sed --in-place=.bak -e` / `perl -pi -e` / `perl -i.bak -pe` each produce one write naming the edited file.\\n- `tee f.md < in.txt`, `cp a.md b.md`, `cp -Rc src dist`, `cp -t specs/x a.md b.md`, `mv a.md b.md`, `rm -f a.md b.md` (two writes), `mkdir -p specs/x/y`, `touch -t 202601010101 f.md` all name the right target.\\n- `cd specs/x && sed -i 's/a/b/' report.md` names `specs/x/report.md`; `cat doc.md | tee notes.md` names `notes.md`.\\n- `grep -rn 'rm a.md' f.md`, `echo 'cp a b'`, `sed -n '1,5p' f.md`, `git commit -m \\\"docs; rm stale notes\\\"` produce no write.\\n- `sh -c 'rm a.md'` and `bash -lc \\\"sed -i 's/a/b/' f.md\\\"` reach the nested command.\\n- `commandLines`: plain, numbered, numbered-with-bracket, heading, checkbox, bold-wrapped and inline-code reports are read; a prose quote, blockquote, three-backtick fence, tilde fence and a fenced report are skipped; `/deep:review` plus `/deep:review:auto` tally as two lines of one command and `repeatedCommands` returns 1.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"A refusal or a sentence that quotes the marker is read as a start\\\": ruled out. `The model printed COMMAND: /deep:review → started in its reply.` returns no line, and a line that opens with `>` returns none.\\n- \\\"`sed -i.bak` or `perl -i.bak` loses the edited file\\\": ruled out. The script word is marked and the file survives in both readers.\\n- \\\"`cp -t dest src.md` names the source\\\": ruled out; the probe prints `dest` and the test pins it.\\n- \\\"The mode-suffix tally double-counts one command\\\": ruled out; `commandLines` and `repeatedCommands` both key on namespace and name.\\n- \\\"A quoted separator inside a commit message becomes a write\\\": ruled out; `git commit -m \\\"docs; rm stale notes\\\"` emits no write.\\n- \\\"The new write branch drops a redirect target\\\": ruled out; a call with both a redirect and an in-place writer emits the redirect target first, then the writer's targets.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus area: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` source checks and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` live-turn guard\\n- Reason: the brief's next three checks are provenance (dirty source, stale build, escaping/absolute link,\\n  JSON line on a failed check) and the every-turn remote check with no network push\\n- Rotation status: first pass on these files this round\\n- Required evidence: the refusal order in `main`, the marker lines and their readers, `turnRefusal`'s call\\n  site and the `childEnv` overrides, plus the README rows that describe them\\n- Recovery note: not applicable\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781197957,"end":1794781231694}}}}
