{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781326781,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","part":{"partID":"prt_1e14d959600221khB7La2JdWPM","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","messageID":"msg_1e14d8884001slG39RYOpnas1P","type":"tool","id":"call_58e9f18e34254235ade2e392","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 7. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the new `shellWriteTargets` block against the plan's D1 writer table word by word\n  surfaced the exact spelling each writer branch handles before any test was read. (iteration 1)\n- Calling `normalize` and `commandLines` in memory on one-call records gave a table of spellings\n  that separated the writers D1 named from the ones it did not, without running the suite. (iteration 1)\n- Reading the long-target test rather than its title showed the assertion checks existence, not the\n  path, which is why the misnamed copy survived. (iteration 1)\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Nothing failed in iteration 1: both readers are pure functions reachable from an in-memory probe,\n  so every case in the findings was reproduced directly. (iteration 1)\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n- The wrapper class (`sudo`, `timeout`, `command`, `env`, `find -exec`, `xargs`, `ssh`, `watch`) reads\n  as no write; recorded by report-3 Q2 and D13, not re-reported. (iteration 1)\n- `**COMMAND:**` and a four-space indented report line were already recorded by D13; not re-reported. (iteration 1)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n## 10. NEXT FOCUS\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` source checks and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` live-turn guard\n- Reason: the brief's next checks are provenance (dirty source, stale build, escaping or absolute link,\n  a JSON line on a failed check) and the every-turn remote check with no network push\n- Rotated from: correctness (iteration 1 complete)\n- Required evidence: the refusal order in `main`, the marker lines and their readers, `turnRefusal`'s\n  call site, the `childEnv` overrides, and the README rows that describe them","oldString":"## 7. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the new `shellWriteTargets` block against the plan's D1 writer table word by word\n  surfaced the exact spelling each writer branch handles before any test was read. (to fill)\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n- (none yet)\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n- none yet\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n## 10. NEXT FOCUS\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: shell write reader and COMMAND line reader in `score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n- Reason: the brief names both readers first; they carry the P1 the fix closes and the P2s it\n  must not reopen\n- Required evidence: `sed -i`/`perl -i`/`tee`/`cp`/`mv`/`rm`/`mkdir`/`touch` spellings through\n  `normalize`, a quoted marker and a fenced marker through `commandLines`","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -104,29 +104,37 @@\n \n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Reading the new `shellWriteTargets` block against the plan's D1 writer table word by word\n-  surfaced the exact spelling each writer branch handles before any test was read. (to fill)\n+  surfaced the exact spelling each writer branch handles before any test was read. (iteration 1)\n+- Calling `normalize` and `commandLines` in memory on one-call records gave a table of spellings\n+  that separated the writers D1 named from the ones it did not, without running the suite. (iteration 1)\n+- Reading the long-target test rather than its title showed the assertion checks existence, not the\n+  path, which is why the misnamed copy survived. (iteration 1)\n \n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n \n-- (none yet)\n+- Nothing failed in iteration 1: both readers are pure functions reachable from an in-memory probe,\n+  so every case in the findings was reproduced directly. (iteration 1)\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n-- none yet\n+- The wrapper class (`sudo`, `timeout`, `command`, `env`, `find -exec`, `xargs`, `ssh`, `watch`) reads\n+  as no write; recorded by report-3 Q2 and D13, not re-reported. (iteration 1)\n+- `**COMMAND:**` and a four-space indented report line were already recorded by D13; not re-reported. (iteration 1)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n \n ---\n \n ## 10. NEXT FOCUS\n \n-- Dimension: correctness\n-- Focus area: shell write reader and COMMAND line reader in `score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n-- Reason: the brief names both readers first; they carry the P1 the fix closes and the P2s it\n-  must not reopen\n-- Required evidence: `sed -i`/`perl -i`/`tee`/`cp`/`mv`/`rm`/`mkdir`/`touch` spellings through\n-  `normalize`, a quoted marker and a fenced marker through `commandLines`\n+- Dimension: security\n+- Focus area: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` source checks and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` live-turn guard\n+- Reason: the brief's next checks are provenance (dirty source, stale build, escaping or absolute link,\n+  a JSON line on a failed check) and the every-turn remote check with no network push\n+- Rotated from: correctness (iteration 1 complete)\n+- Required evidence: the refusal order in `main`, the marker lines and their readers, `turnRefusal`'s\n+  call site, the `childEnv` overrides, and the README rows that describe them\n","status":"modified","additions":17,"deletions":9}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the new `shellWriteTargets` block against the plan's D1 writer table word by word\\n  surfaced the exact spelling each writer branch handles before any test was read. (iteration 1)\\n- Calling `normalize` and `commandLines` in memory on one-call records gave a table of spellings\\n  that separated the writers D1 named from the ones it did not, without running the suite. (iteration 1)\\n- Reading the long-target test rather than its title showed the assertion checks existence, not the\\n  path, which is why the misnamed copy survived. (iteration 1)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Nothing failed in iteration 1: both readers are pure functions reachable from an in-memory probe,\\n  so every case in the findings was reproduced directly. (iteration 1)\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n- The wrapper class (`sudo`, `timeout`, `command`, `env`, `find -exec`, `xargs`, `ssh`, `watch`) reads\\n  as no write; recorded by report-3 Q2 and D13, not re-reported. (iteration 1)\\n- `**COMMAND:**` and a four-space indented report line were already recorded by D13; not re-reported. (iteration 1)\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Focus area: `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` source checks and `run-command-behaviour.mjs` live-turn guard\\n- Reason: the brief's next checks are provenance (dirty source, stale build, escaping or absolute link,\\n  a JSON line on a failed check) and the every-turn remote check with no network push\\n- Rotated from: correctness (iteration 1 complete)\\n- Required evidence: the refusal order in `main`, the marker lines and their readers, `turnRefusal`'s\\n  call site, the `childEnv` overrides, and the README rows that describe them\",\"oldString\":\"## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the new `shellWriteTargets` block against the plan's D1 writer table word by word\\n  surfaced the exact spelling each writer branch handles before any test was read. (to fill)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- (none yet)\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n- none yet\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: shell write reader and COMMAND line reader in `score-command-transcripts.mjs`\\n- Reason: the brief names both readers first; they carry the P1 the fix closes and the P2s it\\n  must not reopen\\n- Required evidence: `sed -i`/`perl -i`/`tee`/`cp`/`mv`/`rm`/`mkdir`/`touch` spellings through\\n  `normalize`, a quoted marker and a fenced marker through `commandLines`\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781320598,"end":1794781326781}}}}
