{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781566041,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","part":{"partID":"prt_1e1514cfa0019w7gi9O7W3L3wu","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","messageID":"msg_1e1513191001lwLYCXKdilQtyk","type":"tool","id":"call_c06404becafc4dfd8d3f2cc3","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"   Case: a live turn runs `rm -rf .git` in the arena; the next turn's `turnRefusal` runs `git -C <arena> remote`, git exits 128, and the arm ends with a stack trace and exit 1 instead of `{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"arena_unprepared\"}`. Before this phase the guard ran only before the first turn, so the exposure existed once per arm; now it exists before every turn.","oldString":"   Case: a live turn runs `rm -rf .git` in the arena; the next turn's `turnRefusal` runs `git -C <arena> remote`, git exits 128, and the arm ends with a stack trace and exit 1 instead of `{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"arena_unprepared\"}`. Before this phase the guard ran only before the first turn, so the exposure existed once per arm; now it exists before every turn.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md\n@@ -45,9 +45,8 @@\n    Finding class: correctness\n    Scope proof: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:618-654` and `:1296-1299`, inside the declared accuracy-runner path; the every-turn call is the new code this round confirms.\n    Affected surface hints: the arm loop (`:1428-1430`), the run log (a throw writes no refusal line), and the operator-facing exit code (1 instead of 2).\n    Case: a live turn runs `rm -rf .git` in the arena; the next turn's `turnRefusal` runs `git -C <arena> remote`, git exits 128, and the arm ends with a stack trace and exit 1 instead of `{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"arena_unprepared\"}`. Before this phase the guard ran only before the first turn, so the exposure existed once per arm; now it exists before every turn.\n-\n 2. **A mid-arm refusal names no row, so the stop cannot be tied to the log's last line** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:1429` -- `runArm` writes `result.refusal` and returns, and `liveArmRefusal`'s object holds only `code` and `remotes` (:633). The `head_moved` refusal beside it carries `rowId` (:1360), so the two mid-arm stops report differently.\n    Finding class: traceability\n    Scope proof: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1408-1433`, the arm loop the every-turn guard now interrupts.\n    Affected surface hints: the arm's JSON refusal and the run log; a later summary reads the short log without a stop marker (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:2462` sets `armIncomplete` from per-row run counts, not from the selection size).\n","status":"modified","additions":0,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-confirm-5b/iterations/iteration-002.md (1 replacement)"}],"p