/` as the text. Change the comment above `SHELL_COMMAND_FLAG` and `nestedCommand` to say the shell or `eval` must be the segment's command, after any runner. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with every earlier case unchanged, `TC` exits 0, `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs` prints the lines of `probes-after.txt`, and `G diff HEAD -- $S` shows no change to `isShellWriter`, `SHORT_FLAG_IN_PLACE`, `PERL_IN_PLACE` or `PERL_ARGUMENT_SWITCH`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T050e.md): first run 5 failed incl. mkdir -p eval reports and echo eval rm a.md, then 330/330, typecheck 0, probe 8/8, no table write lost against d0f605b42f8 beyond the four allowed; eight wrapper forms (bash -o pipefail -c, sudo bash -c and others) read as no write, as before the rebuild, recorded as a known limit\n101:- [x] T006 [P] Let the builder own the marker name (`CBG` and `COT`, then `B`, `R` and `CO`). After T002. Test first: in `CBG` add `import { MARK } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs'`, a case `the arena marker name is the builder's` that asserts `MARK` is `skilled-behaviour-arena`, and write the marker at line 286 with `MARK`. In `COT` import `MARK` the same way and write the marker at line 573 with it. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail because the builder exports no `MARK`. Then in `B` export `MARK`, add `copyArgs` nowhere yet, and wrap the `main(process.argv.slice(2))` call in the `invokedDirectly` guard `R` uses at lines 1482 to 1491, with the same comment shape. In `R` delete `const MARK` and import it from `./prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, and in `CO` import it and use `join(checkoutDir, '.git', MARK)` in `trustedCheckout`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c \"'skilled-behaviour-are