sts/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c 'probe-032' $CBG` prints nothing and `LEFT` prints 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T011.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n107:- [x] T012 Check for a remote before every live turn (`CBG`, then `R`). After T011. Test first, in `CBG`: on a temporary repository with the marker written with `MARK`, `turnRefusal(dir, { dryRun: false })` returns `null`, after `git remote add origin file:///nonexistent.git` it returns `{ ok: false, code: 'remote_present', remotes: ['origin'] }`, and `turnRefusal(dir, { dryRun: true })` returns `null` with the remote still there. Run the test and see it fail because `R` exports no `turnRefusal`. Then export `turnRefusal(root, { dryRun })` from `R`, returning `null` on a dry run and `liveArmRefusal(root)` otherwise, call it in `runTurn` before the `if (isFirst)` block with the refusal returned as it is today, and keep the dirty-path check inside that block. Change the comment above `liveArmRefusal` at lines 610 to 613 and the one in `runTurn` at lines 1267 to 1269 so they say a remote is what a turn could push to by name and the push boundary is `childEnv`'s empty credential helper, empty `GH_CONFIG_DIR` and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, as `plan.md` D3 states. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed, `sed -n '/^async function runTurn/,/if (isFirst)/p' $R | rg -c 'turnRefusal\\(REPO_ROOT'` prints 1, `rg -n 'the one way a turn reaches outside' $R` prints nothing, and `node $V5/remote-guard.mjs` prints the lines of `probes-before.txt`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T012.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n108:- [x] T013 Narrow the builder header (`B`). After T012. A comment change with no behaviour to test. Change the header sentence at lines 5 to 10 that says a live turn cannot reach anything outside its own checkout, so it says the arena takes away remotes, an outer repository's hooks and credentials, while the filesystem stays reachable by absolute path, as `plan.md` D3 states. Verify: `rg -c 'cannot reach anything outside' $B` prints nothing, `node --check $B` exits 0, `G diff -U0 -- $B | rg '^\\+\\s*//' | rg -c 'specs/|[0-9]{3}-[a-z]|\\bD[0-9]+\\b|\\b(T|P|Q)[0-9]{3}\\b'` prints nothing, and `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T013.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n109:- [x] T014 State the builder's refusals and the every-turn guard in the routing-accuracy README (`RA`). After T013. A doc task. In the paragraph at line 111 and the `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` row at line 143, name the three refusals `source_dirty`, `stale_build` and `symlink_escape` with one clause each, the `trackedDotenv` output field and the marker's lines, and in the `run-command-behaviour.mjs` row at line 137 say a live run checks for a remote before every turn. Verify: `rg -c 'source_dirty|stale_build|symlink_escape' $RA` prints at least 1, `rg -c 'trackedDotenv' $RA` prints 1, `DOCV $RA` exits 0 and `G diff -U0 -- $RA | rg '^\\+' | rg -c '\\x{2014}'` prints nothing. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T014.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n110:- [x] T044 Count a build's inputs outside its folder (`CBG`, then `B`). After T014, added by the coordinator from the T039 review's P1, reproduced by the coordinator with the review's input (`ok:true`, arena `hook.ts` v2 beside a `dist` built from v1). Test first, in `CBG`'s `arena builder` block: a clean source that ignores `dist/`, commits `skill/runtime/lib.ts`, `skill/hooks/claude/hook.ts` and `skill/runtime/tsconfig.build.json` holding `{\"include\":[\"**/*.ts\",\"../hooks/**/*.ts\"]}`, w