5:- [x] T035 [C] Run every gate and compare the floors (`$SP/after.txt`, `$SP/floor-after.txt`, `$SP/eval-after.txt`). After every lane and T034, and only while no worker session is open. Run `BUILD`, `TC`, the nine `VX` files of T001, `VALL`, `DT`, `VT`, `VMIR`, `META`, `PBV`, `SHAPE` and `LINKS`, and write each command with its result lines into `after.txt`. Then run `FLOOR > $SP/floor-after.txt` and `EVAL > $SP/eval-after.txt` and `cmp` each with its before file. When `VALL` fails on a timing or load case, rerun that file alone twice and then `VALL` once, and record all three. When a floor or eval line differs, write the moved counts into the parent goal log with `PLOG` and mark the task `[B]`. Verify: every run reports 0 failed, `fail 0` or exit 0, `VALL` reports at least the passed count of `before.txt`, `PBV` prints `scenarios=53` and `violations=0`, `LINKS` prints no more broken links than `before.txt`, and both `cmp` runs print nothing and exit 0. Evidence: scratch/after.txt: BUILD, TC exit 0, nine VX files pass, VALL 185 files 2206 passed (before 2157), DT 1237 pass 0 fail, VT 84 pass, VMIR 3 PASS, META 6 exit 0, PBV scenarios=53 violations=0, SHAPE pass=1, LINKS 0 broken (before 0), floor and eval cmp exit 0\n156:- [x] T036 [C] Rerun the probes (`$SP/probes-after.txt`). After T035. Run `PROBES > $SP/probes-after.txt 2>&1`, then `LEFT`. Then, with the phase's changes still uncommitted, run `T=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR%/}/probe-032.XXXXXX\"); node $B --source . --dest \"$T/arena\"; rm -rf \"$T\"` once. Verify: `probes-after.txt` reads as SC-001 of `spec.md` states: the after lines of REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-005 and REQ-007, the `python write` line and every `remote-guard.mjs` line equal to their before lines, and the builder on this checkout prints `source_dirty` naming only paths in `FILES`, `$PH` or `$PK/goal.md`, which T034's `PLOG` rows changed. `LEFT` prints 0. Evidence: scratch/probes-after.txt: REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-005 and REQ-007 after lines present, python write line and remote-guard lines equal before, wiring-match prints agents_spawn hook-missing exit=1 and main ok exit=0; builder on this checkout: source_dirty naming 10 paths (capped at 10), all in FILES (scratch/arena-dirty.txt); LEFT 0 0\n157:- [x] T037 [C] Check the boundaries (`$SP/boundaries.txt`). After T036. Write each command with its output or exit code into the file. Verify: `G diff --quiet BASE -- AGENTS.md .vibe .skilled/hooks $ADV/lib/advisor-disabled.ts .skilled/bin` exits 0. `test \"$(G rev-parse BASE:$RAD/command-prompts.jsonl)\" = \"$(G hash-object $RAD/command-prompts.jsonl)\"` and the same for `$RAD/holdout-prompts.jsonl` and `$RAD/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl` exit 0. `G diff --quiet BASE -- $RAD/command-routing-baseline.json $RAD/scorer-eval-baseline.json $RL` exits 0. `G diff --stat BASE -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing. `G diff BASE -U0 -- $S $B $R $CO $CTS $CBG $COT $LBT $CSD $VB $VBT $UPS $UPT $HW $HWT $RMC | rg '^\\+\\s*(//|\\*|/\\*)' | rg -c 'specs/|[0-9]{3}-[a-z]|\\b(T|P|Q|A)[0-9]{3}\\b|\\bD[0-9]+\\b|\\b(REQ|AC|CHK|ADR|SC|NFR)-[0-9]+|\\bphase [0-9]+|iter[0-9]-P[0-9]|\\bR[0-9]-P[0-9]-[0-9]{3}|DM5-P[0-9]|(accuracy-runner|kill-switch-cli|vibe-hooks-doctor|docs-metadata)-'` prints nothing. `G diff BASE -U0 -- $RA $ER $GDF $LRM $HK $FM $MTP $CL1 $TRM | rg '^\\+' | rg -c '\\x{2014}'` prints nothing, and the same added lines with no backtick in them, `rg -v '\\x60'`, print no semicolon. `G status --porcelain --untracked-files=all -- .skilled .opencode .github .vibe AGENTS.md` names only `FILES`. `LEFT` prints 0. Each pattern runs directly in the shell, never through a heredoc and `eval`. Evidence: scratch/boundaries.txt: protected paths diff --quiet exit 0, three row files hash equal to BASE, baselines and stored runs unchanged, no package change, 0 added comments naming an id, 0 em dashes and 0 bare semicolons in added doc lines, 28 status paths all in FILES, LEFT 0 0\n158:- [x] T038 [C] Commit the fix (`FILES` and this phase folder). After T037. Stage by path with `G add -- FILES $PH`, never with `-a` or a folder above `$PH`, and commit with a conventional message and a second `-m` prose body. The parent `spec.md`, `../decision-record.md`, `../goal.md` and `../review/` are not part of this commit. Record the short hash as `FIX`. When the commit hook times out on a git call, rerun the commit with `SPECKIT_GIT_TIMEOUT=180` set in front. Verify: `G status --porcelain -- FILES $PH` prints nothing, `G log -1 --format=%h` prints `FIX` and `G show --stat --format= FIX` lists only paths in `FILES` or under `$PH`. Evidence: FIX = d0f605b42f8: 64 files, the 28 FILES paths and the phase folder only (show --name-only), status of FILES and the phase folder clean after the commit; hook warnings on subject and body line length only\n159:- [x] T039 [C] Review the fix diff (`$SP/review/brief.txt`, `$SP/review/report.txt`). After T038. Write `brief.txt` naming the diff `G diff BASE FIX -- FILES`, the REQ tables and the Mechanism per Path table of `spec.md` and decisions D1 to D13 of `plan.md`, and asking whether each writer's target is the word the command writes, whether the anchored `COMMAND:` reader drops a line a model prints as its own, whether the stale rule can pass a build of an uncommitted edit or refuse the committed tree, whether a link check can be raced or skipped, whether `turnRefusal` runs before every live turn, whether each doc row states what its code does, whether a moved stored figure is unexplained, whether an added comment names an id and whether a recorded finding was in fact buildable inside `FILES`. One Opus reviewer reads it read-only and writes `report.txt` with a verdict line and each item at P0, P1 or P2. Reproduce each P0 and P1 by running its cited input. A reproduced one becomes a new task with the next free id in the track that owns the file, test first and checked by an Opus verifier, then a new fix commit whose diff the reviewer reads again. A P1 that does not reproduce is recorded with the command that showed it, and each P2 is recorded on this line with its fix or its reason. Verify: `report.txt` holds a verdict line, and every P0 and P1 it names is named by a task line or recorded here as not reproduced. Evidence: scratch/review/report.txt verdict FIX (P1 1, P2 9). The P1 (stale build blind to tsconfig include folders) reproduced by the coordinator with the review's input (ok:true, hook.ts v2 beside a dist built from v1) and fixed in T044. P2 fixes: Q1 /dev/null T049, Q1 quotes and options T050 to T050e (rebuilt as option D of a Fable 5.2 review after three failed fixes), Q2 markup T051 and T051a, Q4 T046, Q10 T045, Q5 T047, Q6 README T048 and T048a, Q6 hook names T052, Q7 the unsafeNoChangedPath move added to rescore-delta.txt with a PLOG row. P2 reasons: Q2 indented code and the bold label, recorded in plan D13. Fix commits 02261e94254 and d21dbc1cafe. Re-reads: report-2.txt verdict SHIP (0 P0, 0 P1, 6 P2, one fixed in T050e, the rest in D13), report-3.txt verdict SHIP (0 P0, 0 P1, 4 P2, all in D13)\n160:- [ ] T040 [C] Run the re-review round on the fix diff (`$PK/review/review-scope-5b.txt`, `$PK/review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-5b.json`, `$PK/review/review-brief-5b.txt`). After T039. Let `LAST` be the newest fix commit of T038 and T039. Write `review-scope-5b.txt` in the shape of `review-scope-4b.txt`: a header line naming `BASE`, `LAST` and the command, then one line per path of `G diff --name-only BASE LAST -- .skilled .github ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/holdout-prompts.jsonl' ':(exclude)**/behaviour-fresh-prompts.jsonl'`, with the area `accuracy-runner` for the lane A files, `kill-switch-cli` for the lane K files, `vibe-hooks-doctor` for the lane V files and `docs-metadata` for the lane D files. Write `deep-review-fanout-config-pass-5b.json` in the shape of `deep-review-fanout-config-pass-4b.json` with four `cli-opencode` executors on `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort `max`, three iterations each, labelled `accuracy-runner-confirm-5b`, `kill-switch-cli-confirm-5b`, `vibe-hooks-doctor-confirm-5b` and `docs-metadata-confirm-5b`, and concurrency 4. Write `review-brief-5b.txt` from `review-brief-4b.txt`, naming the scope file, the commit range, that this round confirms the fixes for the findings of `review/verify-5/report.md` and looks for defects they added, that a finding the report rejects or a decision of `plan.md` D13 records is not re-reported without a new input that breaks it, and the holdout rule word for word. Run `/deep:review` with that config at threshold 0.10, as pass four ran its round `4b`. Verify: `jq -r '.executors[].label' $PK/review/deep-review-fanout-config-pass-5b.json` prints the four labels, each lineage folder under `$PK/review/lineages/` holds a `deep-review-state.jsonl`, and the last `newFindingsRatio` of each is written into `$SP/review-rounds.txt`.\n\n[showing lines 17-60 of 60; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1e152bd380014FDNklz5DSyhyl.out]","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":true,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"97:- [x] T050e Read nested shell text only from the segment's own command (`CTS`, then `S`). After T051a, added by the coordinator from the second review of the fix (scratch/review/report-2.txt, the `nestedCommand` and `SHELL_COMMAND_FLAG` lines). Test first, in `CTS`, with the builders and the ask row the T050c nested cases use: `mkdir -p eval reports` gives writes `eval` and `reports`, `echo eval rm a.md` and `grep bash -c 'rm x.md' notes.md` give no write, `bash -cx 'rm a.md'` gives one write `a.md`, `env FOO=1 bash -c \"rm a.md\"`, `nohup sh -c 'rm a.md'` and `nice -n 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'` each give one write `a.md`, and `bash script.sh -c 'rm a.md'` gives no write, while every T050c nested case (`bash -c`, `eval`, `timeout 5 bash -lc`) keeps its result. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see `mkdir -p eval reports` miss `reports` or `echo eval rm a.md` give a write. Then in `S`'s `nestedCommand`, skip a leading run of runner words (`timeout` with its option words and its duration, `env` with its option words and `NAME=value` words, `nice` with `-n` and its value, `nohup`, `command`, `exec` and `time`), and read nested text only when the next word is a shell name or `eval`. After a shell name, read option words only until the first word that does not start with `-`, and take the word after the first option matching `/^-[A-Za-z]*c[A-Za-z]*$/` as the text. Change the comment above `SHELL_COMMAND_FLAG` and `nestedCommand` to say the shell or `eval` must be the segment's command, after any runner. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed with every earlier case unchanged, `TC` exits 0, `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs` prints the lines of `probes-after.txt`, and `G diff HEAD -- $S` shows no change to `isShellWriter`, `SHORT_FLAG_IN_PLACE`, `PERL_IN_PLACE` or `PERL_ARGUMENT_SWITCH`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T050e.md): first run 5 failed incl. mkdir -p eval reports and echo eval rm a.md, then 330/330, typecheck 0, probe 8/8, no table write lost against d0f605b42f8 beyond the four allowed; eight wrapper forms (bash -o pipefail -c, sudo bash -c and others) read as no write, as before the rebuild, recorded as a known limit\n101:- [x] T006 [P] Let the builder own the marker name (`CBG` and `COT`, then `B`, `R` and `CO`). After T002. Test first: in `CBG` add `import { MARK } from '../scripts/routing-accuracy/prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs'`, a case `the arena marker name is the builder's` that asserts `MARK` is `skilled-behaviour-arena`, and write the marker at line 286 with `MARK`. In `COT` import `MARK` the same way and write the marker at line 573 with it. Run `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and see it fail because the builder exports no `MARK`. Then in `B` export `MARK`, add `copyArgs` nowhere yet, and wrap the `main(process.argv.slice(2))` call in the `invokedDirectly` guard `R` uses at lines 1482 to 1491, with the same comment shape. In `R` delete `const MARK` and import it from `./prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs`, and in `CO` import it and use `join(checkoutDir, '.git', MARK)` in `trustedCheckout`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-offer.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c \"'skilled-behaviour-arena'\" $RAD $ADV/tests` prints one line, for `B`, with count 1, `node $B; echo $?` prints the usage line and 2, `node --input-type=module -e \"const m = await import('./$B'); console.log(typeof m.MARK)\"` prints `string` and creates no folder, and `bash $SP/planning/arena-cases.sh \"$PWD/$B\"` prints the five lines of `probes-before.txt`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T006.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n102:- [x] T007 Refuse a dirty source and a stale build, and record the source status in the marker (`CBG`, then `B`). After T006. Test first, in `CBG`'s `arena builder` block, with a source that ignores `dist/`, commits `src.js` and holds `dist/out.js`, its times set with `utimesSync`: a source whose `src.js` changed after the commit exits 2 with stdout code `source_dirty` and no arena folder, a clean source whose `dist/out.js` is older than `src.js` exits 2 with `stale_build` and no arena folder, and a clean source whose build is newer exits 0 with a marker of three lines, the head, `source clean` and a line that starts `built dist `. Run the test and see exit 0 on the first case. Then in `B`'s `main`, before the clone and in this order, refuse `source_dirty` with the first ten paths when `git status --porcelain` in the source prints a line, and refuse `stale_build` naming every stale folder, each with its newest source time and its build time, when a `dist` in `copyPlan` is older than the newest file `git ls-files -z -- <its folder>` lists outside that folder's `dist/` and `node_modules/`, as `plan.md` D2 states. Write the marker as the head, `source clean` and one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied `dist`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed with the two existing builder cases still passing, `bash $SP/planning/arena-cases.sh \"$PWD/$B\"` prints `A exit=2 {\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"source_dirty\"}`, `B exit=2 {\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"stale_build\"}` and `D exit=0 {\"ok\":true,\"code\":null} marker-lines=3 marker-second-line=source_clean`, and `bash $V5/arena-provenance.sh \"$PWD/$B\"` prints `builder exit=2` for its cases A and B. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T007.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n103:- [x] T008 Refuse a copied link that leaves the source (`CBG`, then `B`). After T007. Test first, in `CBG`: a clean source with a fresh build whose `dist/linked` points to a folder outside the source exits 2 with `symlink_escape` and no arena folder, a `dist` link to a dangling target exits 2 the same way, and a `dist/inner` link to a file inside the source is copied as a link. Run the test and see exit 0 on the first case. Then in `B`'s `main`, before the clone, walk each tree `copyPlan` names once and refuse `symlink_escape` with the link's path when its real path is outside the source or cannot be resolved, as `plan.md` D5 states. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed and `arena-cases.sh` prints `C exit=2 {\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"symlink_escape\"} outside-readable=no`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T008.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n104:- [x] T009 Name tracked dotenv files (`CBG`, then `B`). After T008. Test first, in `CBG`: a clean source with a fresh build that commits `.env.example` exits 0 with `trackedDotenv` `[\".env.example\"]` in its output and a marker line `tracked-dotenv .env.example`, and a source without one prints no `trackedDotenv` field. Run the test and see no field. Then in `B` list each file `git ls-files` prints at the head whose base name matches `DOTENV_PATTERN`, add it to the success output only when the list is not empty and write one `tracked-dotenv <path>` marker line each, and change the header sentence at lines 31 to 34 so it says the skip covers the copied build trees, because a clone brings every tracked file, as `plan.md` D6 states. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed, `arena-cases.sh` prints `E exit=0 {\"ok\":true,\"code\":null,\"trackedDotenv\":[\".env.example\"]} arena-has-env-example=yes` and its line D shows no `trackedDotenv`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T009.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n105:- [x] T010 Pass the clonefile flag on macOS only (`CBG`, then `B`). After T009. Test first, in `CBG`: `copyArgs('darwin')` equals `['-Rc']` and `copyArgs('linux')` equals `['-R']`. Run the test and see it fail because `B` exports no `copyArgs`. Then export `copyArgs(platform)` from `B` and pass `copyArgs(process.platform)` in `runCp`, and change the comment above `copyPath` so it says the flag is macOS only. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed and `rg -n \"'-Rc'\" $B` prints one line, inside `copyArgs`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T010.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n106:- [x] T011 Test the copy path (`CBG`). After T010. Add a case to the `arena builder` block: a clean source that ignores `dist/` and holds a fresh `dist/out.js`, `dist/sub/deep.js` and `dist/.env.local` builds with exit 0, the arena's `dist/out.js` and `dist/sub/deep.js` equal the source's, the arena has no `dist/.env.local`, the output's `copied` names `dist`, and the arena's `dist/out.js` time is not earlier than the time taken just before the build. Falsifiability: copy `B` to a `probe-032` folder, delete the line `if (DOTENV_PATTERN.test(entry.name)) continue;` from the copy, point the case's builder path at it for one run, see the dotenv assertion fail, then restore the path and remove the folder in the same command. Verify: the mutated run fails on the dotenv assertion, then `VX tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c 'probe-032' $CBG` prints nothing and `LEFT` prints 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T011.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n107:- [x] T012 Check for a remote before every live turn (`CBG`, then `R`). After T011. Test first, in `CBG`: on a temporary repository with the marker written with `MARK`, `turnRefusal(dir, { dryRun: false })` returns `null`, after `git remote add origin file:///nonexistent.git` it returns `{ ok: false, code: 'remote_present', remotes: ['origin'] }`, and `turnRefusal(dir, { dryRun: true })` returns `null` with the remote still there. Run the test and see it fail because `R` exports no `turnRefusal`. Then export `turnRefusal(root, { dryRun })` from `R`, returning `null` on a dry run and `liveArmRefusal(root)` otherwise, call it in `runTurn` before the `if (isFirst)` block with the refusal returned as it is today, and keep the dirty-path check inside that block. Change the comment above `liveArmRefusal` at lines 610 to 613 and the one in `runTurn` at lines 1267 to 1269 so they say a remote is what a turn could push to by name and the push boundary is `childEnv`'s empty credential helper, empty `GH_CONFIG_DIR` and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, as `plan.md` D3 states. Verify: the first run fails a