49, added by the coordinator from the T039 review (Q1, quotes and options). Test first, in `CTS`, same builders and row: `git commit -m \"docs; rm stale notes\"` and `echo \"a | tee b\"` give no `write` event, `mkdir \"my dir\"` gives one write naming `my dir`, `mkdir -m 755 dir` and `mkdir --mode=755 dir` give one write naming `dir`, `touch -r ref.md f.md` and `touch -t 202601010000 f.md` give one write naming `f.md`, `cp -t dest src.md` and `mv -t dest src.md` give one write naming `dest`, `sed -i 's/a/b/' f1.md f2.md` and `perl -pi -e 's/a/b/' f1.md f2.md` give two writes naming `f1.md` and `f2.md`, and `sed -i -e 's/a/b/' f1.md` gives one write naming `f1.md`. Run the test and see the quoted `git commit` read as a write. Then in `S` split each command into parts and each part into words with one quote-aware scan in the manner of `redirectTargets` (a separator or space inside single or double quotes is text, and the quotes are removed from the word), skip the word after `-m` for `mkdir`, after `-t`, `-d` and `-r` for `touch` and after `-e` and `-f` for `sed` and `perl`, take the word after `-t` as the one target of `cp` and `mv`, and for `sed` and `perl` record every file word after the script, where the script is the first non-option word when no `-e` or `-f` was given. Keep `cd` folde\n- [x] T050a Read an inline sed or perl script as given (`CTS`, then `S`). After T050, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T050. Test first, in `CTS`, same builders and row: `perl -pi -e's/a/b/' f.md` and `sed -i --expression='s/a/b/' f.md` each give one write naming `f.md`, `sed -i -e's/a/b/' f1.md f2.md` gives two writes naming `f1.md` and `f2.md`, and `perl -i -pe 's/a/b/' f.md` still gives one write naming `f.md`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the `perl -pi -e's/a/b/'` case give a `shell` event. Then in `editedWords` count the script as given when a word is `-e` or `-f`, starts with `-e` or `-f` and carries its script inline, or starts with `--expression=` or `--file=`, and skip the next word only for a bare `-e`, `-f`, `--expression` or `--file`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, every T050 case still passes, `TC` exits 0 and `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs` prints the lines of `probes-after.txt`. Evidence: Opus verifier FAIL then fixed by T050b (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T050a.md): first run 3 failed as the line names, then 249/249, typecheck 0, probe 8/8; a script inside a short-option cluster still read as no write, superseded by T050c\n- [x] T050b Read a script carried inside a short-option cluster (`CTS`, then `S`). After T050a, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T050a. Test first, in `CTS`, same builders and row: `perl -i -pe's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i.bak -pe's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -pi -we's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i -ne'print' f.md`, `perl -pi -E's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -i -Ee's/a/b/' f.md` and `sed -i -ne's/a/b/p' f.md` each give one write naming `f.md`. `perl -i -pe's/a/b/' AGENTS.md` gives a write with `unsafe` true on an ask row. `perl -i -pe 's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -ie 's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -i.bak 's/a/b/' f.md` and `sed -i -E 's/a/b/' f.md` still give one write naming `f.md`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the `perl -i -pe's/a/b/' f.md` case give a `shell` event. Then in `editedWords`, which receives the writer, read each short-option word letter by letter. Stop at `i`, because the rest of the word is the backup suffix. For perl, also stop at a letter that takes an inline argument, the ones `PERL_ARGUMENT_SWITCH` names plus `0` and `l`. When the scan reaches a script letter, the script is given: it is inline when text follows the letter, and it is the next word, which is skipped, when the letter ends the word. The script letters are `e` and `f` for sed, and `e` and `E` for perl, so sed's `-E` stays a plain option. Keep the bare `-e`, `-f`, `--expression`, `--fil\n- [x] T050c Keep quotes on shell words and read sed and perl from HEAD's flags (`CTS`, then `S`). After T050b, which it supersedes, added by the coordinator from the stop-after-three decision (option D of a Fable 5.2 review, kept in scratchpad fable-t050). Test first, in `CTS`, same builders and ask row. Every existing T003, T003a, T049, T050, T050a and T050b case stays as written and none is removed. Add these cases. Read-only, one `shell` event each: `perl -ne'print' f.md`, `perl -ne'print if /x/' AGENTS.md` and `perl -pe'print' AGENTS.md` (each also `unsafe` false), `perl -le'print 1' f.md`, `sed -ne'/visible/p' f.md`, `perl -ne 'print' f.md`, `sed -n -e '/a/p' f.md`. One write naming `f.md` each: `perl -i -lpe's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i -lane'print' f.md`, `perl -i -0pe's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i -F: -lane'print' f.md`, `perl -pi -e 's/a/b/' -e 's/c/d/' f.md`, `sed -i --expression 's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -i --file=s.sed f.md`, `sed -i -fs.sed f.md`, `sed --in-place=.bak -e 's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -0777 -pi -e 's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -pi -E 's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i -lpe 's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -lpi -e 's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i -Mstrict -pe's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -pie 's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -i -nf s.sed f.md`, `sed -i -nfs.sed f.md`, `sed -ni -e 's/a/b/p' f.md`, `sed -i -Ef s.sed f.md`, `sed -i --posix 's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -i --debug -e 's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i -pe's/a/b/' -- f.md`, `perl -i -pe\n- [x] T050d Name the `'\\''` splitter case as the T050c line gives it, and correct the in-place comment (`CTS`, then `S`). After T050c, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T050c. In `CTS`, in the `reads only the changed files after $name` table, set the `a closed quote beside an escaped one` command to the JS string `\"sed -i 's/it'\\\\''s/its/' f.md\"`, which is the shell text `sed -i 's/it'\\''s/its/' f.md`, and set the `a trailing comment` command to `\"rm a.md # it's gone\\ntouch b.md\"`, with no space before `touch`. Keep both rows' expected paths. `S` already gives one write `f.md` for the first and writes `a.md` and `b.md` for the second, at HEAD and in the working tree, so the first run is expected to pass and no failing run is required. In `S`, change only the comment above `SHORT_FLAG_IN_PLACE` so it says these patterns decide whether a sed or perl call edits in place, read on the quoted words, while `editedWords` picks the files. Verify: `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and 315 tests, every earlier case is unchanged, `rg -c -F \"s/it'\\\\\\\\''s/its/\" $CTS` prints at least 1 (corrected from an under-escaped pattern the verifier flagged), `TC` exits 0, and `G diff HEAD -- $S` shows no change to `isShellWriter`, `SHORT_FLAG_IN_PLACE`, `PERL_IN_PLACE` or `PERL_ARGUMENT_SWITCH` apart from that comment. Evidence: Opus verifier PA\n- [x] T051 Read the opening markup and fences a model prints (`CTS`, then `S`). After T050, added by the coordinator from the T039 review (Q2). Test first, in `CTS`'s `commandLines` block: `1) COMMAND: /deep:review → started`, `### COMMAND: /deep:review → started` and `- [x] COMMAND: /deep:review → started` each give one line, a `COMMAND:` line between two `~~~` lines gives none, and a `COMMAND:` line between two ``` lines indented six spaces under a list item gives none, while the existing cases keep their results. Run the test and see the `1)` case give none. Then widen `COMMAND_LINE`'s opening markup to allow `\\d+[.)]` list numbers, a `#{1,6}` heading run and a `[ ]` or `[x]` checkbox after a list marker, and change `FENCE_LINE` to match ``` or `~~~` after any indentation, a fence closing only on its own character. Change the comment above `COMMAND_LINE` to name the new markup. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints the lines of `probes-after.txt`. Evidence: Opus verifier FAIL then fixed by T051a (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T051.md): first run 5 failed including 1) giving none, then 320/320, typecheck 0, command-line probe lines 9 to 13 match; a checkbox counted without a list marker, fixed in T051a\n- [x] T051a Read a checkbox only after a list marker (`CTS`, then `S`). After T051, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T051. Test first, in `CTS`'s `commandLines` block: `[x] COMMAND: /deep:review → started` with no list marker gives no line, and `1) [x] COMMAND: /deep:review → started` gives one line, while every existing case, `- [x] COMMAND: /deep:review → started` included, keeps its result. In the same edit, change the comment above the indented-fence case from \"indented past the four spaces a quote may carry\" to \"indented past the three spaces a top-level fence may carry\". Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the bare `[x]` case give one line. Then in `S` change `COMMAND_LINE`'s opening repeat to `(?:(?:[-*+]|\\d+[.)])[ \\t]+(?:\\[[ xX]\\][ \\t]+)?|#{1,6}[ \\t]+|[`*_\\[])*`, so a checkbox counts only right after a list marker, and leave the rest of the pattern, `FENCE_LINE` and `commandLines` unchanged. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0 and `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints lines 9 to 13 of `probes-after.txt`. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T051a.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n- [x] T050e Read nested shell text only from the segment's own command (`CTS`, then `S`). After T051a, added by the coordinator from the second review of the fix (scratch/review/report-2.txt, the `nestedCommand` and `SHELL_COMMAND_FLAG` lines). Test first, in `CTS`, with the builders and the ask row the T050c nested cases use: `mkdir -p eval reports` gives writes `eval` and `reports`, `echo eval rm a.md` and `grep bash -c 'rm x.md' notes.md` give no write, `bash -cx 'rm a.md'` gives one write `a.md`, `env FOO=1 bash -c \"rm a.md\"`, `nohup sh -c 'rm a.md'` and `nice -n 5 bash -c 'rm a.md'` each give one write `a.md`, and `bash script.sh -c 'rm a.md'` gives no write, while every T050c nested case (`bash -c`, `eval`, `timeout 5 bash -lc`) keeps its result. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see `mkdir -p eval reports` miss `reports` or `echo eval rm a.md` give a write. Then in `S`'s `nestedCommand`, skip a leading run of runner words (`timeout` with its option words and its duration, `env` with its option words and `NAME=value` words, `nice` with `-n` and its value, `nohup`, `command`, `exec` and `time`), and read nested text only when the next word is a shell name or `eval`. After a shell name, read option words only until the first word that does not start with `-`, and take the word after the first option matching `/^-[A-Za-z]*c[A-Za-z]*$/` as the text. Change\n\n### Lane A, arena track: the builder and the runner\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '85,100p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md | cut -c1-1400\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781672162,"end":1794781672876}}}}
