{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794781685695,"sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","part":{"partID":"prt_1e15325a4001m5jgJ0PvztxrAE","sessionID":"ses_e1ebd75ccffe6y3ELjfB5p5w0O","messageID":"msg_1e152fac40010wjlxhQ35Qh5qo","type":"tool","id":"call_27b99a00ef7f4183b95c223f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '80,85p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md | cut -c1-1200"},"output":"### Lane A, scorer track: the transcript scorer\n\n- [x] T003 [P] Read an in-place shell edit as a write (`CTS`, then `S`). After T002. Test first, in `CTS`, with the builders its cases already use and an `ask` row expecting `/deep:review`: for each of `sed -i '' 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `sed -i 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `sed --in-place 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `perl -pi -e 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `echo x | tee specs/x/review/report.md`, `cp /tmp/a specs/x/review/report.md`, `mv /tmp/a specs/x/review/report.md` and `touch specs/x/review/report.md` as one Claude `Bash` call, `normalize` gives one event of kind `write` with that path, `startState` gives `unsafe: true` and `loopInit` gives `false`. Add four more cases: `rm -f a.md b.md` gives two writes in order, `mkdir -p specs/x/review` gives one write naming the folder, `echo x | tee` gives one `shell` event, and `cp .skilled/commands/deep/review.md /tmp/out.md` gives one write naming `/tmp/out.md` and never the document. Add two parity cases: `cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md | tee notes.md` and `cp .skilled/commands/deep/review.md x.md` each give what `cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md > notes.md` gives, kinds `write` and `starte\n- [x] T003a Drop redirect words from the write targets and anchor the perl in-place test (`CTS`, then `S`). After T003, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T003. Test first, in `CTS`: `cp /tmp/a specs/x/review/report.md 2>/dev/null` and `sed -i '' 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md 2>&1` each give one write naming `specs/x/review/report.md`, `echo x | tee specs/x/review/report.md > /dev/null` gives one write naming the report, and `perl -Mstrict -ne 'print' notes.md` and `perl -Ilib -e 1 notes.md` each give one `shell` event. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the `2>/dev/null` case fail on path `2>/dev/null`. Then in `shellWriteTargets` skip any word that opens with an optional digit and `>`, `>>`, `>&`, `&>` or `<`, and the word after a bare redirect operator. For perl count only `-i`, a word starting `-i`, or a cluster of argument-free switches ending at `i` (`-pi`, `-0pi`, `-ni`), never a word starting `-M`, `-m`, `-I`, `-x` or `-e`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs` prints the same eight lines as after T003, and `TC` e\n- [x] T004 Read a `COMMAND:` line only where the model printed it as its own (`CTS`, then `S`). After T003. Test first, in `CTS`: the probe's refusal text `A line like COMMAND: /deep:review → started appears only when I actually run one, so you will not see it here.` gives `commandLines` `[]` and `startState` with `started: false`, a line `> COMMAND: /deep:review → started` gives `[]`, and a `COMMAND: /deep:review → started` line between two lines of three backticks gives `[]`. Every line form an existing `CTS` case accepts stays accepted, and one new case adds `1. COMMAND: /deep:review → started`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the refusal case fail with one entry. Then in `commandLines` skip a line inside a fence and a line that opens with `>`, and accept `COMMAND:` only at the start of a line after optional whitespace, list markers, a number with a dot, emphasis markers, a backtick or a square bracket, as `plan.md` D4 states, with the module comment above `COMMAND_LINE` saying so. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed and `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints `quoted marker commandLines []`, `quoted marker startedC\n- [x] T004a Reset the fence state per text block (`CTS`, then `S`). After T004, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T004. Test first, in `CTS`: a session of two turns, the first with text \"```bash\\necho hi\" and the second with text `COMMAND: /deep:review → started`, gives `commandLines` `[{ seq: 1, command: '/deep:review', state: 'started', count: 1 }]`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see that case fail with `[]`. Then in `commandLines` move `let fenced = false` inside the `for (const event of events ?? [])` loop, so each text event starts outside a fence. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints the same five lines as after T004, and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T004a.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Lane A, scorer track: the transcript scorer\n\n- [x] T003 [P] Read an in-place shell edit as a write (`CTS`, then `S`). After T002. Test first, in `CTS`, with the builders its cases already use and an `ask` row expecting `/deep:review`: for each of `sed -i '' 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `sed -i 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `sed --in-place 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `perl -pi -e 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md`, `echo x | tee specs/x/review/report.md`, `cp /tmp/a specs/x/review/report.md`, `mv /tmp/a specs/x/review/report.md` and `touch specs/x/review/report.md` as one Claude `Bash` call, `normalize` gives one event of kind `write` with that path, `startState` gives `unsafe: true` and `loopInit` gives `false`. Add four more cases: `rm -f a.md b.md` gives two writes in order, `mkdir -p specs/x/review` gives one write naming the folder, `echo x | tee` gives one `shell` event, and `cp .skilled/commands/deep/review.md /tmp/out.md` gives one write naming `/tmp/out.md` and never the document. Add two parity cases: `cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md | tee notes.md` and `cp .skilled/commands/deep/review.md x.md` each give what `cat .skilled/commands/deep/review.md > notes.md` gives, kinds `write` and `starte\n- [x] T003a Drop redirect words from the write targets and anchor the perl in-place test (`CTS`, then `S`). After T003, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T003. Test first, in `CTS`: `cp /tmp/a specs/x/review/report.md 2>/dev/null` and `sed -i '' 's/a/b/' specs/x/review/report.md 2>&1` each give one write naming `specs/x/review/report.md`, `echo x | tee specs/x/review/report.md > /dev/null` gives one write naming the report, and `perl -Mstrict -ne 'print' notes.md` and `perl -Ilib -e 1 notes.md` each give one `shell` event. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the `2>/dev/null` case fail on path `2>/dev/null`. Then in `shellWriteTargets` skip any word that opens with an optional digit and `>`, `>>`, `>&`, `&>` or `<`, and the word after a bare redirect operator. For perl count only `-i`, a word starting `-i`, or a cluster of argument-free switches ending at `i` (`-pi`, `-0pi`, `-ni`), never a word starting `-M`, `-m`, `-I`, `-x` or `-e`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs` prints the same eight lines as after T003, and `TC` e\n- [x] T004 Read a `COMMAND:` line only where the model printed it as its own (`CTS`, then `S`). After T003. Test first, in `CTS`: the probe's refusal text `A line like COMMAND: /deep:review → started appears only when I actually run one, so you will not see it here.` gives `commandLines` `[]` and `startState` with `started: false`, a line `> COMMAND: /deep:review → started` gives `[]`, and a `COMMAND: /deep:review → started` line between two lines of three backticks gives `[]`. Every line form an existing `CTS` case accepts stays accepted, and one new case adds `1. COMMAND: /deep:review → started`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the refusal case fail with one entry. Then in `commandLines` skip a line inside a fence and a line that opens with `>`, and accept `COMMAND:` only at the start of a line after optional whitespace, list markers, a number with a dot, emphasis markers, a backtick or a square bracket, as `plan.md` D4 states, with the module comment above `COMMAND_LINE` saying so. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed and `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints `quoted marker commandLines []`, `quoted marker startedC\n- [x] T004a Reset the fence state per text block (`CTS`, then `S`). After T004, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T004. Test first, in `CTS`: a session of two turns, the first with text \"```bash\\necho hi\" and the second with text `COMMAND: /deep:review → started`, gives `commandLines` `[{ seq: 1, command: '/deep:review', state: 'started', count: 1 }]`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see that case fail with `[]`. Then in `commandLines` move `let fenced = false` inside the `for (const event of events ?? [])` loop, so each text event starts outside a fence. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints the same five lines as after T004, and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T004a.md): test-first run and the line's Verify checks observed by the verifier\n"}],"providerC