it names, with `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside that folder, and with `symlink_escape` when a link inside a copied tree resolves outside the source or names an absolute path that still resolves inside it. It writes the marker as the head, then `source clean`, then one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied build tree and one `tracked-dotenv <path>` line per tracked dotenv file.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"001-command-routing-baseline-corpus\n002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata\n003-plain-chat-command-reach\n004-command-meaning-matching\n005-recommendation-contract-and-brief\n006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost\n009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research\n010-reachability-and-attribution\n011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n012-plain-offer-reach\n013-attribution-and-install-reach\n014-review-remediation\n015-health-default-and-brief-refinements\n016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n017-review-pass-two-remediation\n018-holdout-row-retirement\n019-workflow-outcome-measure\n020-command-offer-fit-guards\n021-brief-head-parity\n022-workflow-measure-soundness\n023-untuned-outcome-evidence\n024-fable-review-remediation\n025-release-notes-and-doc-sync\n026-untuned-behaviour-arm\n027-review-pass-four-remediation\n028-direct-call-off-switch\n029-direct-call-kill-switch\n030-vibe-runtime-parity\n===\n`prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` leaves a `CLAUDE.md` holding `@AGENTS.md` in an arena that has none and appends `/CLAUDE.md` to `.git/info/exclude`, so Claude Code imports the arena's own rules while the clean-tree check and the head stay as they were. Before it copies anything it refuses the source with `source_dirty` when a tracked or untracked edit would leave the arena unlike the commit it names, with `stale_build` when a copied `dist` is older than the newest tracked file in the folder that holds it or in a folder its tsconfig `include` reaches outside that folder, and with `symlink_escape` when a link inside a copied tree resolves outside the source or names an absolute path that still resolves inside it. It writes the marker as the head, then `source clean`, then one `built <relPath> <ISO time>` line per copied build tree and one `tracked-dotenv <path>` line per tracked dotenv file.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/ | head -30; echo ===; sed -n '111p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794781736594,"end":1794781737432}}}}
